ndow I think at one point the water  was up to like here  some New York residents are now asking  themselves how much longer they can go  on living here as the climate becomes  more and more extreme and the sea level  continues to rise  one possible solution is to try and hold  back the waves with the sea wall and  that's exactly what they're doing here  the city is spending billions of pounds  on flood defenses I'm meeting Thomas one  of the leading Engineers so Lila  following superstorm Sandy what we came  up with is a sea wall that runs all  around the southern tip of Manhattan  it's about 10 miles long we looked at it  and we thought about wave action and the  potential for water still splashing over  the wall which is why we're coming up to  an elevation which is about nine feet  higher than where we're standing right  now  so here's the thing flood defenses are  great but some people think they're just  a sticking plaster and eventually a bit  like with my sand castle the rising sea  levels will do their damage  so do we need a more radical solution to  save our coastal cities and ultimately  to save Humanity  well how about this an incredible vision  of the future like something out of a  movie Welcome to the world's first  floating city  so this is just a computer-generated  animation showing what it might look  like but believe it or not a city like  this could soon become a reality I'm  meeting the chief engineer from a  company called oceanx which is hoping to  build the world's first floating city in  South Korea the advantage of 14 seating  is we can move up and down with the ways  and with the tides and the feather is  floating it's also helpful because it  will accommodate the sea water level  rising but how can you make a city float  won't like the buildings and everything  be just way too heavy well it follows a  certain physical principle which is the  one that is used by boats right they are  very heavy but they still float so is  this an excepti